   "text": "Calculate the percentage total body surface area (% TBSA) burnt using the figure below.",
   "bbox": [
    260.5,
    89.5,
    581.4,
    99.7
   ],
   "key": "p31-0dfc3aef"
  },
  {
   "id": "p31-out-e03",
   "page": 31,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Approach to the patient with burn/s not needing urgent attention • Cool burn < 3 hours old with cool tap water or wet towel for 30 minutes and give single dose paracetamol 1g for pain before cleaning wound. • Remove loose/dead skin and gently clean burn with chlorhexidine 0.05% or sodium chloride 0.9%. Then cover with paraffin gauze dressing. • Give tetanus toxoid 0.5mL IM if none in past 5 years. • If cigarette burns, burn with specific shape (e.g. iron, grid, knife/fork, car cigarette lighter, light bulb), repeated/unexplained burns/other unexplained injuries, consider abuse 33 and self-harm 34. • Give paracetamol 500mg-1g 4-6 hourly (up to 4g in 24 hours) as needed for up to 5 days. • Review daily until burn healed: - Dress burn with paraffin gauze dressing. If signs of infection (redness, swelling), apply povidone iodine 5% cream daily. - If severe infection (extensive redness or swelling, foul-smell, pus or temperature ≥ 38°C), pain despite medication or burn not healed after 2 weeks, refer.",
   "bbox": [
    51.0,
    435.9,
    785.2,
    527.1
   ],
   "key": "p31-c4a41afb"
  },
  {
   "id": "p31-out-e04",
